2026-06-03T03:38Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0206 made `erg spec` / `erg integration` print-on-demand and stopped
init from depositing tickets/spec-erg-v1.md and tickets/integration.md; init
now removes them as orphans when they match a known embedded hash. But
git-erg's OWN tickets/ still git-tracks tickets/spec-erg-v1.md (and possibly
tickets/integration.md) from before 0206. The /verify on PR #249 (ticket 0213)
flagged these as stale tracked orphans that drift from the embedded source --
they are no longer deployed by init, so keeping them tracked is dead weight and
will diverge silently from src/go/assets/.

Note: 0206's orphan cleanup only removes them on `erg init` when they match a
known embedded hash; if git-erg's tracked copies have drifted they would be
preserved -- and either way a tracked file must be removed with `git rm`, not
left to init.

## Actions

1. Confirm which of tickets/spec-erg-v1.md, tickets/integration.md are still
   git-tracked in git-erg (`git ls-files tickets/`).
2. `git rm` the tracked orphan(s). They remain available via `erg spec` /
   `erg integration` and embedded under src/go/assets/.
3. Check no doc/test references the deleted tracked paths (README, tests,
   test_roundtrip already drop them; re-grep to be sure).

## Test

`tests/test_selfcoherence.sh` already asserts the deployed set is exactly the 2
retained assets (.ergrc, AGENTS.md); after removal, optionally tighten it to
assert tickets/spec-erg-v1.md and tickets/integration.md are NOT tracked.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Stale tracked tickets/spec-erg-v1.md / integration.md removed via git rm.
- [ ] `erg spec` and `erg integration` still print the content (embedded).
- [ ] No dangling reference to the removed tracked paths.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
